 ## A field named claim
 
 On my E-E-A-T post, four of the five significance runs returned no scores at all. That looked like the laziness I'd predicted. It wasn't. The score field was called claim, and Haiku read it as "describe the claim": it wrote sentences where the numbers should go. Claude renamed the fields to importance_score, evidence_score and empty_score and made the tool schema strict. All five runs came back complete.
 
+*Figure: Two rows of five answer slips. Under the field name claim, four slips are filled with lines of sentences and one holds a number. Under importance_score, all five hold a number.*
